# READ-FIELD-CLOSURE (Codex K03-READ-FIELD-CLOSURE-20261008-31, -29 step 3: write/address): Model's code passes
# the address of node\x -- x's cell in its node, not a hidden input's local -- to put, which writes 5 through it.
# b, a merge of Model, runs with a copy of the unit as its node that holds x as the merge saw it: put writes the
# copy's x cell (5, the post paths), and the unit's x cell stays 3; u, which nothing copied reads, is absent from
# the copy.  Exit 7; 82 if b's k is not put's 0.
int: x 3
int: u 9
fn: put (@: int p) int
    \p: 5
return: 0
Model:
    int: k 1
    k: put(@ node\x)
end: Model
b: merge: Model
b
int: ok 7
if: b\k != 0
    ok: 82
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
